  "title": "Meeting of Altan Khan and Sonam Gyatso at Qinghai Lake, 1578",
  "summary": "In summer 1578 the Tumed Mongol ruler Altan Khan met the Gelug teacher Sonam Gyatso near Kokonur (Qinghai Lake) and gave him the title Dalai Lama. The two renewed a priest and patron relationship, and the title was later applied to two predecessors, making Sonam Gyatso the third. Gelug Buddhism then spread widely among the Mongols.",
